{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "27fabddf-f86e-4083-b212-489e3654d265",
    "name": "TriloPlan Backend API",
    "description": "Backend API for the video-chat platform (User app, Host app, Admin app). See BACKEND_PLAN.md, BRD.md and DEVELOPMENT_ROADMAP.md in the repo for full context.\n\n## Status (as of this export)\nBuilt and live: Phase 0 (foundations), Phase 1 (auth + profiles), Phase 3 (host discovery + presence).\nNot yet built: Phase 2 (wallet/recharge — pending payment gateway decision), calls, live broadcasting, gifting, withdrawals, admin panel.\n\n## Auth flow\n1. Run **Auth — Login** top to bottom: it requests+verifies an OTP for a USER phone, then requests+verifies an OTP for a HOST phone. Whichever Verify OTP ran most recently becomes your \"current session\" — the `accessToken`/`refreshToken`/`userId` collection variables — used automatically by every other request via the collection's Bearer auth.\n2. In non-production environments (this one, right now), OTP responses include `devCode` — auto-saved to a collection variable by a test script, since there's no real SMS provider wired up yet.\n3. Access tokens expire after 15 minutes. Use **Auth — Session → Refresh Access Token** to get a new pair — the old refresh token is invalidated the moment you do, so it's single-use.\n\nThis whole collection is safe to run top-to-bottom via Collection Runner: Auth — Login leaves you authenticated as the HOST test account, so Profile and Hosts folders (including the host-only endpoints) succeed; Auth — Session (Refresh, then Logout) is deliberately placed last so it doesn't clear your session before you've exercised everything else.\n\n## Known limitations right now\n- OTP delivery is dev-mode only (logged + returned as `devCode`) — no real SMS provider configured yet.\n- KYC document submission expects a `documentUrl` you already have — there's no presigned-upload endpoint yet since object storage (S3/R2) isn't wired up.\n- Presence is in-memory on a single server instance for now (will move to Redis once that's provisioned) — functionally identical for testing purposes.\n- Presence toggles also broadcast a `presence:update` event over Socket.io to connected clients. Postman can't easily demonstrate that (it's not a plain HTTP call) — connect with `auth: { token: <accessToken> }` and listen for `presence:update` to see it live from a frontend client.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [],
