        {
          "name": "Submit KYC Document",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"documentUrl\": \"https://example.com/id-proof.pdf\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/kyc",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["me", "kyc"]
            },
            "description": "Records that a KYC document was submitted and moves `kycStatus` to `pending`. An admin will review and approve/reject it later (admin review workflow is Phase 9, not yet built).\n\nCURRENT LIMITATION: this endpoint expects `documentUrl` to already point at an uploaded file — there's no presigned-upload endpoint yet since object storage (S3/R2) credentials aren't configured. Until that lands, the frontend needs some other way to get a URL here for testing (e.g. any publicly reachable file URL works for now, since nothing validates the content, only that it's a well-formed URL)."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "OK",
              "originalRequest": {
